        <mxCell id="-jTMe1FUypn5eOMLOyxl-3" value="1. \(f_1\) (Hz) - Supply Frequency &#xa;   - The fundamental electrical frequency applied to the stator windings.&#xa;&#xa;2. \(f_r\) (Hz) - Shaft Rotational Frequency &#xa;   - The frequency at which the motor shaft rotates.&#xa;&#xa;3. \(s\) (unitless) - Slip&#xa;   - Indicates how much slower the rotor is compared to the stator field.&#xa;&#xa;4. \(p\) (unitless) - Number of Pole Pairs &#xa;   - Defines the number of magnetic pole pairs in the motor.&#xa;&#xa;5. \(R_s\) (unitless) - Stator Slot Number&#xa;   - The total number of stator slots.&#xa;&#xa;6. \(D_{\text{pit}}\) (meters) - Pitch Diameter&#xa;   - The mean diameter of the bearing raceway.&#xa;&#xa;7. \(D_{\text{ball}}\) (meters) - Rolling Element Diameter  &#xa;   - The diameter of each rolling element (ball or roller).&#xa;&#xa;8. \(\beta\) (radians) - Contact Angle&#xa;   - The angle between the rolling element and the bearing races.&#xa;&#xa;9. \(n\) (integer) - Number of Rolling Elements&#xa;   - Total number of rolling elements (balls or rollers) in the bearing." style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontStyle=0;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
